/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# The two Cross-Origin-* lines are what make SharedArrayBuffer available, which
# is what lets the tool use the fast multi-threaded video core. Remove them and
# everything still works, just roughly two to three times slower per video.
#
# They also mean every cross-origin file has to be fetched with CORS. That is
# already handled in the page: the Google Fonts stylesheet and the JSZip script
# both carry crossorigin, and the ffmpeg core is fetched with fetch() and turned
# into a blob URL.
